1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,378
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:06,673
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,476
[Ibyang] <i>What did Aunt Cita say?</i>

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,895
[Ame] <i>We won't be with her anymore.</i>

8
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:21,813
She's gone.

9
00:00:21,896 --> 00:00:23,231
PREVIOUSLY

10
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:24,691
[Janine] <i>I feel guilty.</i>

11
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:26,818
- Were you with Atoy?
- [Janine] No.

12
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:29,738
[Ibyang] <i>You should have brought</i>
<i>Sister Tonet to Tatoy.</i>

13
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:31,364
Maybe she wouldn't have been
in an accident.

14
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,199
Maybe she'd still be alive!

15
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,284
You're so selfish!

16
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,910
[Emerson, in English] <i>Freak accident?</i>

17
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:38,621
<i>The scaffolding fell on her?</i>

18
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:40,248
[Red] <i>What's your problem? Tonet's dead.</i>

19
00:00:40,331 --> 00:00:41,666
It's my first time killing someone.

20
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,917
[Martina, in English]
<i>I've never done that!</i>

21
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:44,377
You killed her for a good reason.

22
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,545
[Mercado] <i>What's this for, Padua?</i>

23
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:46,713
[Atoy] <i>Just a personal mission, sir.</i>

24
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:48,381
<i>My assistant, Tonet…</i>

25
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:51,342
I suspect what happened to her
wasn't an accident.

26
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:54,512
[Atoy] <i>What did the man and woman</i>
<i>who accused her look like?</i>

27
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:58,141
[security guard]
<i>Sir, the man was tall, fair-skinned.</i>

28
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:00,977
<i>And the woman</i>
<i>was beautiful, had round eyes.</i>

29
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,062
<i>They said they were married.</i>

30
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:03,688
[Atoy] <i>Can I see that?</i>

31
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:05,482
[security guard]
<i>The computer system crashed</i>

32
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,524
<i>when the fire alarm went off.</i>

33
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:10,028
<i>All the recorded files</i>
<i>from that day were erased.</i>

34
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:11,571
Unless someone deleted them.

35
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:13,073
[Dmitri, in English] <i>Wait.</i>
<i>What happened to your bag?</i>

36
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,657
[Martina] <i>I just noticed this now.</i>

37
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,208
[music fades]

38
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:24,667
[crickets chirping]

39
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,296
What happened to that rock stud?

40
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:31,716
It doesn't just come off easily.

41
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,010
[anxious music playing]

42
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:35,595
[in English] Not unless…

43
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:37,347
[grunting]

44
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:42,310
Could I have left it there?

45
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:44,479
Is this what you're looking for?

46
00:01:44,562 --> 00:01:46,314
[music swells]

47
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:49,984
[frantic music playing]

48
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:52,278
[screaming]

49
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:57,408
[panicked breathing]

50
00:01:57,492 --> 00:01:58,785
[Red] Hon. Hon!

51
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,036
- [gasping]
- [Red groans]

52
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,704
[mysterious music playing]

53
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:04,415
- [in English] What's wrong?
- [gasping]

54
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,669
- Tonet stabbed me!
- [Red groans]

55
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:08,920
[in English] Right here!

56
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:10,630
[in English] Why is she in my dreams now?

57
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,300
You're just thinking about it too much.

58
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:15,218
[sighs]

59
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:16,761
What can I do?

60
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,307
‪[sighs]

61
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,350
[in English] You know what?

62
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:26,688
Maybe you should go to the wake tomorrow.
Go with Audrey.

63
00:02:27,355 --> 00:02:29,732
[in English] No. That's not
gonna help me get over it.

64
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:33,611
Yes, I know. But… get some news there.

65
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:37,323
Maybe she told someone else what she knew.

66
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:41,077
Maybe they still want to investigate
her death, right?

67
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,705
Find out what's on their mind.

68
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:46,833
Find out what's on Atoy's mind.

69
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:48,334
[in English] Why-- Why Atoy?

70
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:50,587
[in English] He's a tracker.

71
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,338
So, he's like a spy.

72
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:55,550
He probably has another theory
about Tonet's death.

73
00:02:56,676 --> 00:03:00,263
It's better that we know already,
before he starts to suspect.

74
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:03,600
[rousing music playing]

75
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:06,603
[sauve theme music playing]

76
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,494
[clacking]

77
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:34,380
[music fades]

78
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:36,299
[man] My condolences.

79
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:38,218
[woman] Sir, our condolences.

80
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:41,763
[muffled chattering]

81
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:45,266
'Son.

82
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:53,107
Emerson, my condolences.

83
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:55,193
Do you need anything? Have you eaten?

84
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:57,528
- [Emerson] Yes.
- [Paldo] Bro.

85
00:03:58,029 --> 00:04:01,157
Here's your favorite pares,
from Brother Kurt.

86
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:05,411
Condolences, Emerson.

87
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:07,038
We also offer our condolences.

88
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:11,084
Bro, a tight hug.

89
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:14,379
[somber music playing]

90
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:20,927
Thank you.

91
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:27,558
Emerson, we know you're alone now.

92
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:30,812
But we won't let you feel alone.

93
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:32,981
If we can help with anything,
just let us know.

94
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:34,315
What do you need?

95
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:38,361
[melancholic music playing]

96
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:41,990
I need to have…

97
00:04:42,907 --> 00:04:45,868
formal clothes made for Tonet.

98
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,372
She doesn't have anything for the burial.

99
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,480
[knock on door]

100
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,316
[Siony] Emerson?

101
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:21,988
Bro, here's the fabric you need.

102
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:24,907
Do you need anything else?

103
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:30,496
Nothing more. Thank you.

104
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:32,290
We're here for you.

105
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:40,006
[sentimental music playing]

106
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:46,345
There's only one person…

107
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:49,307
important to me that I don't want to lose.

108
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:51,684
Who?

109
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,812
- You! You're so silly.
- [laughs]

110
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:58,232
- Who else! Who else would it be?
- [laughs]

111
00:05:58,316 --> 00:05:59,233
All right.

112
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:00,401
Okay, okay, okay.

113
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,779
So dramatic! You're so dramatic.

114
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:04,238
- It's fine.
- There's global warming.

115
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:05,448
This is the first time
we've hugged like this.

116
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:06,741
Okay, okay, okay.

117
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:08,242
[in English] I love you too.
I love you too.

118
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:11,245
[sentimental music playing]

119
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:13,915
- [Peping] Emerson.
- [Emerson sniffs]

120
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:20,421
- [man] 'Son, here.
- Thank you.

121
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:24,675
Here.

122
00:06:29,013 --> 00:06:31,641
[melancholic music playing]

123
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:32,767
Are you okay?

124
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,562
I'm fine now. I'm okay, thank you.

125
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:45,488
[inaudible]

126
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:20,440
[music fades]

127
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:27,488
Bro. Emerson.

128
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:30,199
You haven't eaten yet.

129
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:32,535
I'm fine.

130
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:34,454
[melancholic music playing]

131
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:35,872
I brought you coffee.

132
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:37,999
I'll put it here.

133
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:43,337
[Kurt] This is Bicol Express.

134
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:44,797
That's my secret recipe.

135
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:47,800
[Emerson] I'm fine.

136
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:49,844
Just put it there.

137
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:03,900
[sewing machine whirring]

138
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:12,783
It's beautiful, Emerson!

139
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:15,536
Tonet will surely love this.

140
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,581
[melodramatic music playing]

141
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:25,963
Too bad she won't see what I made.

142
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:30,009
[Emerson sobs]

143
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:36,140
I didn't even make her anything.

144
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:40,895
But at least…

145
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,817
At least she can still wear…

146
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,780
wear… [sobs]

147
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:51,948
what I sewed.

148
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:02,416
[softly] You made something beautiful.

149
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:09,006
[sobs, then sighs]

150
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:14,178
[softly] You made something beautiful.

151
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:15,513
[chuckles softly]

152
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,027
[music fades]

153
00:09:30,611 --> 00:09:33,489
Now I understand how you felt when…

154
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:37,827
you made clothes
for Sir Delfin, for his wake.

155
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,080
[melancholic music playing]

156
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:44,208
Somehow, I'm happy that I made…

157
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:48,754
[voice breaks] I made a dress for Tonet.

158
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:49,714
I just--

159
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:50,715
[sobs]

160
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:55,219
I just didn't know it would be like this…

161
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:59,056
That I'd be making her burial clothes.

162
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:04,353
[sobbing]

163
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,277
It hurts so much.

164
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,528
It hurts.

165
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:18,284
Because just when we got reunited,
she was taken from me right away.

166
00:10:18,367 --> 00:10:20,578
[sobbing]

167
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:21,621
[Emerson] It hurts.

168
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:27,710
Bro, God has a reason why
she was taken from you so soon.

169
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:34,759
[sobs, then sighs]

170
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:43,434
I suspect…

171
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:48,689
Tonet's death wasn't an accident.

172
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:52,693
- [mysterious music playing]
- [dramatic sting]

173
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:57,782
What do you mean?

174
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:00,493
Was there foul play?

175
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,371
It seems someone else was there.

176
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:08,376
Maybe a woman, but…

177
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:12,129
I'm not sure.

178
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:20,054
How can you say that?

179
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:23,849
[suspicious music playing]

180
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:27,728
Because I went back to the place
where she died.

181
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:33,776
I smelled the perfume of…

182
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:35,986
[music swells]

183
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:37,988
…a woman who…

184
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:42,034
[Atoy] <i>I found a piece of evidence</i>

185
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:43,702
<i>that she might have left behind.</i>

186
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:44,912
[music swells]

187
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:51,210
[birds chirping]

188
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,797
[somber music playing]

189
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,173
[Tonet] <i>Don't worry.</i>

190
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,675
I'll take care of you.

191
00:11:58,926 --> 00:12:02,471
I really hate seeing you cry.

192
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:07,935
Because you know, I love you so much!

193
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:09,019
[dramatic sting]

194
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,730
Ibyang, help me fix this.

195
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:14,525
This is heavy.

196
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,194
Ibyang, are you okay?

197
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,328
Ibyang?

198
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:33,627
I already miss Sister Tonet.

199
00:12:35,379 --> 00:12:36,797
Me too.

200
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:41,510
What hurts more is that I was so useless
the last time we talked.

201
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:45,764
I wish I had good memories with her.

202
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,602
What did you and Sister Tonet talk about

203
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:51,187
before she passed?

204
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:53,814
[Ibyang] <i>Please don't close</i>
<i>your eyes, okay?</i>

205
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:57,401
- Don't close your eyes, okay? [sobbing]
- [gasping]

206
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,987
Sister, don't close your eyes.

207
00:13:00,070 --> 00:13:03,157
You-- You have lunch with Brother Emerson!

208
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,242
Ja… Janine…

209
00:13:06,535 --> 00:13:07,536
Janine…

210
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:11,207
Janine… Janine. She's not…

211
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:15,252
She's not-- She's not…

212
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:19,215
Hmm.

213
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:23,928
She mentioned Janine.

214
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:27,014
She said, "She's not…"

215
00:13:27,097 --> 00:13:28,599
[suspicious music playing]

216
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:29,892
She's not what?

217
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:34,480
That's all. Then she lost consciousness.

218
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:40,069
Of all people, why was Janine
the last person she thought of

219
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:41,570
before she died?

220
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:59,338
[mysterious music playing]

221
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,219
Is this really the wake?

222
00:14:05,844 --> 00:14:08,556
It should've been at a funeral home,
so there's air conditioning.

223
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,933
[in English] Will you shut it, Martina?

224
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,935
[in English] Nobody asked you to be here.

225
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:14,186
[in English] I'm just saying.

226
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,854
It would've been better there, right?

227
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:18,065
[in English] Mom, please be nice.

228
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:19,984
I know Tonet, okay?

229
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,403
We're not close, but we have history.

230
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:25,364
[in English] Can you guys give me a break?

231
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:26,991
I won't do anything to her.

232
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,204
[in English] Come on, Gavin. Let's go.

233
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:36,917
[indistinct chattering]

234
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,085
[man] Massage me a little harder.

235
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:39,336
[man 2] Who won?

236
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,462
This guy here.

237
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:41,589
[indistinct chattering]

238
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:43,549
Emerson?

239
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,677
[in English] Emerson, I'm so sorry.

240
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,887
We offer our condolences.

241
00:14:48,721 --> 00:14:52,808
[in English] This is my sister-in-law,
Martina, and her son, Gavin.

242
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,185
- [in English] Condolence.
- [in English] My condolences.

243
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:58,647
[suspicious music playing]

244
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,066
[Emerson] Thank you for your sympathy.

245
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,776
[dramatic stinging]

246
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:06,530
- Um…
- You're Red's wife?

247
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:08,407
[dramatic sting]

248
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:13,954
[in English] Uh, I'm so sorry
for your loss.

249
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:16,707
[in English] I can only imagine
how tragic this must be for you.

250
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,626
Especially the way Tonet died.

251
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:21,086
[in English] She was such a lovely girl.

252
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:24,965
[Emerson] Yes, it was an accident. She…

253
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:28,177
She lost too much blood and then…

254
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,846
organ failure.

255
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,599
Will you sue? The mall?

256
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:36,602
Because she died on the premises, right?

257
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:40,898
Hmm, we haven't thought about that yet.

258
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:43,817
Auntie, excuse me.

259
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:45,402
All right.

260
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:47,571
[music swells]

261
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,951
Ah, sorry…

262
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:55,079
I just got distracted by your bag.
It's beautiful.

263
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,164
[in English] Oh, thank you!

264
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:59,458
[in English] It's my, uh, favorite one,
my lucky bag.

265
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:00,542
Your favorite?

266
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:03,796
But it looks like…

267
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:06,298
like something's missing.
It looks a little damaged.

268
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:10,511
It seems like it's missing a stud,
like… this?

269
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:13,389
It looks like it might fit. Let's see if--

270
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:14,515
[Martina, in English]
I don't-- I don't think that's gonna fit.

271
00:16:14,598 --> 00:16:16,976
This brand has
a lot of knockoffs being sold.

272
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,603
- [Atoy] Ah. Is that so?
- [Martina titters]

273
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:22,398
[in English] Um, I'm just
gonna get a drink. Excuse me.

274
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:24,274
[tense music playing]

275
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:25,234
[Atoy] Oh?

276
00:16:25,776 --> 00:16:27,820
Where were you all day yesterday?

277
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,613
Were you at a mall?

278
00:16:30,322 --> 00:16:33,283
The same mall
where Tonet had her accident?

279
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:36,745
[in English] Shopping?

280
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:40,207
[intense music playing]

281
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,173
Wait--

282
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:49,591
Hold on. What's happening here?

283
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,343
- [Paldo] Atoy.
- [in English] Let me go.

284
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:52,594
[in English] Why are you asking me
such things?

285
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:55,347
Nothing. I'm just curious. Just asking.

286
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:58,434
I wasn't at the mall yesterday. Okay?

287
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:00,894
- You weren't shopping?
- [in English] No.

288
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:02,521
Where were you?

289
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:03,939
[Martina, in English] What is this about?

290
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:05,983
[suspicious music playing]

291
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:07,568
Because I saw this

292
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:11,530
at the place where Tonet had her accident.

293
00:17:11,613 --> 00:17:12,614
Here.

294
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,408
It just looks a bit… similar…

295
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:17,619
Maybe it just looks alike, right?

296
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:20,122
Huh? Because it could be this.
Oh, it could be this.

297
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:21,582
Maybe it's just coincidence, right?

298
00:17:21,665 --> 00:17:23,083
Who knows? We don't know.

299
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,002
[dramatic sting]

300
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:27,880
And your perfume.

301
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:33,260
Oh. [sniffs]

302
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:35,262
Your favorite too?

303
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:36,346
It smells good.

304
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:41,185
[grunting]

305
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:45,147
What do you guys think?

306
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:49,610
What about you? What do you think?
Was Tonet's death really an accident?

307
00:17:49,693 --> 00:17:51,653
Huh? What do you think?

308
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:54,615
- [Paldo] What's going on here?
- [scoffs]

309
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,493
You know, I want to be offended.

310
00:17:57,576 --> 00:17:58,452
But it's funny.

311
00:17:58,535 --> 00:18:00,579
[in English] This is a bit silly
and pathetic, don't you think?

312
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,748
Don't call us pathetic!

313
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:04,124
[tense music playing]

314
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:07,002
Atoy's instincts are never wrong.

315
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:09,296
So, where were you?

316
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:13,050
Were you there, where my sister died?

317
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:16,595
Huh? Were you the one
who killed my sister?

318
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:17,638
[Atoy] Emerson!

319
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,431
Did you kill my sister?! You killed--

320
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:20,974
- You killed my sister?!
- [clamoring]

321
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:23,227
- [Martina, in English] Let me go!
- Ha?! You monster!

322
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:24,353
You killed my sister!

323
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:26,105
[in English] How dare you!?
I could sue you for assault!

324
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,606
- [Paldo] Stop it!
- [Emerson] Do it!

325
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:28,607
You have no shame!

326
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:31,652
Did you come here just to make sure
that my sister was killed?!

327
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:33,320
I came here to respectfully
offer condolences!

328
00:18:33,403 --> 00:18:35,072
[in English] And then, you're gonna
accuse me of such things?!

329
00:18:35,155 --> 00:18:36,949
[in English] Over what evidence?!
My perfume and my bag?!

330
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:38,117
What are you, psychic?!

331
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,034
Enough. Enough of that!

332
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,078
[woman] You know what, miss? Just leave!

333
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:43,205
[people] Yes! Leave! Leave now!

334
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:45,040
- [clamoring]
- Stop it! Enough already.

335
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,375
- [clamoring]
- [Emerson] Not a criminal?

336
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,585
You are a criminal! I'll prove it!

337
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,129
I'll have you jailed, you animal!

338
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:52,548
[in English] Well, you'd better get
yourself a good lawyer then!

339
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:57,511
- [clamoring]
- [intense music playing]

340
00:18:58,387 --> 00:18:59,888
[people] Criminal! Criminal!

341
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:01,974
[dramatic stinging]

342
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,522
- Get out of here!
- Hey!

343
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:11,150
Shut up! What's wrong with you?!

344
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:12,526
Don't get involved.

345
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:14,945
That's my boss' wife!

346
00:19:23,036 --> 00:19:25,414
- [Gavin] Karla.
- What are you doing here?

347
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:27,332
Offering condolences.

348
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,626
Why didn't you tell me?

349
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,336
I only found out from my aunt.

350
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:33,172
It's okay.

351
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:36,175
I know you were on a date with Cathy.

352
00:19:36,758 --> 00:19:38,093
[in English] Sorry.

353
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:39,803
[in English] I should have
been there for you.

354
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:42,639
But we're still friends, right?

355
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,559
- Let me help you with that.
- No, don't.

356
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:47,144
- [Gavin] No, I want to help.
- It's okay. No--

357
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:48,228
- No, it's okay.
- Hey.

358
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:49,521
Look what you've done.

359
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:50,439
- [Gavin sighs]
- [sighs]

360
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:54,359
- I already said don't.
- Give it to me.

361
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:57,112
[pensive music playing]

362
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:59,072
Hey, boy! So, it's you, huh?

363
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:01,283
I saw you earlier.

364
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:04,161
You were with those two women
who killed Tonet!

365
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:07,289
We didn't do anything wrong.

366
00:20:07,372 --> 00:20:08,916
Tonet was my friend.

367
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:11,460
Psst, make him leave.
Make him leave, right now!

368
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,795
Miss Fely, he didn't do anything.

369
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,839
Leave! Get out of here!

370
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:18,759
Go!

371
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:25,140
That nuisance.

372
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:33,357
Mom, why do they think
you did something to Tonet?

373
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:35,651
[in English] I honestly don't know, Gavin.

374
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:39,363
Maybe they just can't accept
the way your friend died.

375
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:42,783
[in English] You can go ahead now.

376
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:46,328
[somber music playing]

377
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:48,705
[tense music playing]

378
00:20:48,789 --> 00:20:49,915
And you…

379
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:53,669
literally just stood there
and did nothing,

380
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:55,879
while people ganged up on me.

381
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:57,381
That's on you, though.

382
00:20:57,464 --> 00:21:00,884
If you were not making excuses,
you were acting angry.

383
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:04,304
[in English] Wow!
Thank you for that, Audrey.

384
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:07,599
It's just the two of us here.

385
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:08,809
Tell me the truth.

386
00:21:08,892 --> 00:21:10,394
Where were you yesterday?

387
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:12,354
[in English] I was at my office!

388
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:14,064
- At Bahay Kayakap!
- Really?

389
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:17,567
Then why was your bag stud found
where Tonet died?

390
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:18,694
[in English] I don't know, Audrey!

391
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:20,946
I'm not the only one
in the world with bag studs!

392
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,282
[in English] I don't believe you.

393
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:26,868
Why would I kill Tonet?
What's my motivation behind that?!

394
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:29,830
You were the last person she talked to
before she went to the mall!

395
00:21:29,913 --> 00:21:32,791
[in English] Oh my God, Audrey!
You're acting like Atoy!

396
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,501
Now you think you're a detective?!

397
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:35,585
[in English] I'm not a criminal!

398
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:37,671
[in English] But you're married to one!

399
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:40,173
I wouldn't be surprised
if you're just like my brother!

400
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:43,719
Maybe even worse,
because you pretend to be innocent!

401
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:45,971
[in English] How dare you?!

402
00:21:46,054 --> 00:21:47,389
[in English] How dare you?!

403
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,557
[grunting]

404
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,559
[Martina, in English]
I really, really hate you!

405
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:52,728
[grunting and clamoring]

406
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:54,021
- [Red, in English] Enough! Stop!
- [Dmitri, in English] Enough! Stop!

407
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:55,939
- You're not my family!
- [grunts]

408
00:21:56,523 --> 00:21:58,275
What are you two fighting about?!

409
00:21:58,358 --> 00:22:01,236
[in English] She's accusing me of killing
some girl that I don't even know!

410
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,697
That Atoy just stirred things up,
and she believed him!

411
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:04,781
[suspicious music playing]

412
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:06,450
You believe Atoy more than her?

413
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:08,869
Compared to you two? Yes!

414
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:11,872
Because killing isn't new to this family!

415
00:22:11,955 --> 00:22:13,165
- Audrey, my child!
- Stupid!

416
00:22:13,248 --> 00:22:14,291
Audrey!

417
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,545
Whatever happened before, that was then!

418
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:20,672
It's over! We've changed!

419
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:23,300
Maybe you've changed, Dad.

420
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:24,885
I don't know about the others.

421
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:26,386
So, I'm a murderer?

422
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,305
Prove it! Prove it!

423
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:29,765
[in English] Your reaction
just confirms it.

424
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:31,558
- You're stupid!
- [in English] Red, stop it!

425
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,143
[in English] Stop this nonsense!

426
00:22:33,226 --> 00:22:36,104
Dad, it's not nonsense if somebody died!

427
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,272
[tense music playing]

428
00:22:37,355 --> 00:22:38,648
[Red] Then sue me!

429
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:40,734
Go ahead! Don't just keep talking!

430
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:42,277
I said enough already!

431
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:44,196
[Red] Stop siding with her all the time!

432
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:47,032
It's like we never did anything right!

433
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:49,743
Stupid! Let's go!

434
00:22:49,826 --> 00:22:52,996
[intense music playing]

435
00:22:58,502 --> 00:23:00,212
[Red] Why did you even fight with them?

436
00:23:00,295 --> 00:23:02,714
[Martina grunts] They were already
saying harsh words!

437
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:04,800
[in English] You know what?
Audrey is no longer my concern.

438
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:06,259
[in English] It's-- It's that Atoy.

439
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:08,095
[sighs]

440
00:23:08,178 --> 00:23:09,679
[in English] You know,
you asked me to go to that wake,

441
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:12,182
and I just ended up
looking stupid and guilty!

442
00:23:12,265 --> 00:23:13,934
You shouldn't have made me go!

443
00:23:14,434 --> 00:23:15,894
Let it go.

444
00:23:16,728 --> 00:23:19,064
What's important is we know
what Atoy is thinking.

445
00:23:19,856 --> 00:23:21,108
I can handle that.

446
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:22,818
Not just wait for the police
to pick you up.

447
00:23:22,901 --> 00:23:26,363
[mysterious music playing]

448
00:23:27,405 --> 00:23:29,699
[in English] So, what
are you gonna do? Hmm?

449
00:23:31,701 --> 00:23:34,287
The evidence Atoy
gathered against you is weak.

450
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:36,748
The problem is Audrey.

451
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:39,459
[in English] Your sister hates us.

452
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:41,545
[in English] She'll believe
anything that's against us.

453
00:23:44,047 --> 00:23:47,175
But if we can control
what Audrey thinks about you,

454
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:50,762
she could influence Atoy
to stop targeting you, right?

455
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,473
[in English] Hon, you don't know that.

456
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:55,559
Well, let's try.

457
00:23:56,977 --> 00:24:00,647
What's important is you look like…
an innocent victim.

458
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:06,153
The evidence. We need to divert it.

459
00:24:08,446 --> 00:24:09,322
[in English] Okay.

460
00:24:10,907 --> 00:24:12,701
[electronic blipping]

461
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:15,495
[tense music playing]

462
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:24,254
[in English] That Atoy
is biased against Red.

463
00:24:24,337 --> 00:24:27,299
What if he's wrong?

464
00:24:27,382 --> 00:24:29,676
I'm serious. I'll really file
a case against her.

465
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:31,386
What I don't understand is…

466
00:24:31,469 --> 00:24:32,762
UP NEXT

467
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:35,390
…if it's true, then what's her motive?

468
00:24:35,473 --> 00:24:39,186
Was Martina at the office the other day?

469
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:41,855
[in English] Around 12 p.m. onwards?

470
00:24:41,938 --> 00:24:43,481
[Ria] <i>That's the magic of AI.</i>

471
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:45,275
Ma'am, add to my salary, okay?

472
00:24:45,358 --> 00:24:47,527
- Promise me that.
- Of course.

473
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:50,906
Oh, that matches exactly
what we saw Martina carrying,

474
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,449
so she really can't deny it.

475
00:24:52,532 --> 00:24:54,034
[in English] Highly suggestive,

476
00:24:54,117 --> 00:24:58,622
but it does not rise to the level
of establishing criminal liability.

477
00:24:58,705 --> 00:25:01,333
Suspicion alone is insufficient.

478
00:25:01,416 --> 00:25:03,710
Looks like Attorney is right, 'Son.

479
00:25:03,793 --> 00:25:07,422
I wish you hadn't told me your suspicions,

480
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,175
so I wouldn't have hoped for nothing.

481
00:25:10,258 --> 00:25:12,844
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

482
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:16,181
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

483
00:25:16,264 --> 00:25:17,307
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

484
00:25:17,390 --> 00:25:19,142
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
